  regulator and unit approximate delta>|<cell|<verbatim|soften>,
  <verbatim|source>, <verbatim|minus_lap>, <verbatim|source_profile>,
  <verbatim|source_scale>, <verbatim|testing_source>>|<cell|<verbatim|Source.lean>>>|<row|<cell|Exact
  regulated elementary pulse and charge>|<cell|<verbatim|exteriorD>,
  <verbatim|opposite>, <verbatim|cure>, <verbatim|cure_charge>,
  <verbatim|regulated>, <verbatim|reg_pulse>,
  <verbatim|regulated_charge>>|<cell|<verbatim|Regulator.lean>>>|<row|<cell|One
  enclosed coordinate contraction>|<cell|<verbatim|local_force> and its
  <verbatim|pays_reg>/<verbatim|continuous_pays>
  proof>|<cell|<verbatim|Contact.lean>>>|<row|<cell|Higher probe contraction
  on the same fixed collar and drive>|<cell|<verbatim|pulse_differentiated>,
  <verbatim|deriv_flux>, <verbatim|jet_force>>|<cell|<verbatim|Force.lean>>>|<row|<cell|Translation
  and rotation actions>|<cell|<verbatim|variation_value>,
  <verbatim|affine_wave>, <verbatim|variation_drift>, <verbatim|drift_flux>;
  <verbatim|rot_point>, <verbatim|angularLeg>,
  <verbatim|angular_flux>>|<cell|<verbatim|Affine.lean>,
  <verbatim|Angular.lean>>>|<row|<cell|Both legs at the enclosed
  insertion>|<cell|<verbatim|collars_equal>, <verbatim|pulse_hom>,
  <verbatim|two_flux_zero>>|<cell|<verbatim|Repeat.lean>>>|<row|<cell|Exact
  half of ordered double contraction sum>|<cell|<verbatim|front_pair>,
  <verbatim|reads_debit>>|<cell|<verbatim|Double.lean>>>|<row|<cell|Three
  contraction cases and arbitrary complex Wick
  polynomials>|<cell|<verbatim|Motion>, <verbatim|straight_motion>,
  <verbatim|rotational_motion>, <verbatim|fees>,
  <verbatim|moment_force>>|<cell|<verbatim|Taxes.lean>>>|<row|<cell|Actual
  stress polynomial and conservation>|<cell|<verbatim|polStress>,
  <verbatim|stress_label>, <verbatim|pol_conservation>>|<cell|<verbatim|Stress.lean>>>|<row|<cell|Field-table
  Ward identities with common negative coefficient>|<cell|<verbatim|beacon_signal>,
  <verbatim|upper_charge>>|<cell|<verbatim|Beacon.lean>>>|<row|<cell|Reference
  selected before comparisons>|<cell|<verbatim|herald>, <verbatim|shines>,
  <verbatim|maxwell_supplies>>|<cell|<verbatim|Lit.lean>>>>>>

  Also read <verbatim|Lean/YM/UVNext/FREE_STRESS_CERTIFICATE/Choose.lean>:
  <verbatim|YM.UVNext.FreeStress.ignite>, <verbatim|fire>,
  <verbatim|every_light>; and <verbatim|Lean/YM/Pert/Lifted.lean>:
  <verbatim|YM.Pert.address_flat>, <verbatim|address_panel>,
  <verbatim|common_stress>, <verbatim|same_translation>, <verbatim|kappa_eq>.
  The latter proves the numerical coefficient -1 from canonical stress and
  the unchanged derivative plan, not from the mere nonzero coefficient
  returned by <verbatim|fire>.

  The exposition follows the regulator/main source route, rather than
  replacing the source proof by a distributional product argument. The smooth
  source has mass one for four-dimensional Lebesgue measure. Every singular
  product is integrated only on a compact collar away from its poles. Higher
  centre derivatives keep the drive fixed, including for angular motion;
  normalized jet raising factors occur on both sides. The two-enclosed
  contraction uses homogeneity plus collar independence, with exponent
  e-5-j-l\<less\>0. The Wick assembly includes zero, one and two enclosed
  partners and the factor 1/2 from ordered double extraction. The canonical
  polynomial is real/gauge invariant and divergence-free; the low-grade rank
  proof is reused.

  <section|Canonical inputs and boundaries><label|canonical-inputs-and-boundaries>

  Reuses the fixed Maxwell covariance and finite Wick moments from the
  existing free-reference chapters, and <verbatim|trace-free-rank.tex> for
  nonzero stress, onto divergence and its one-dimensional centered kernel.
  <verbatim|actual-stress- normalization.tex> consumes the resulting fixed
  reference certificate. Physical annular Ward representation is a separate
  supplier on the same run. No new proof of the entire reference
  hierarchy/reconstruction or its detector gallery is claimed here. Reference
  packaging keeps the same hierarchy, derivative, rotations, vacuum and
  canonical polynomial; its record assembly does not introduce another
  existential physical family.

  Shared literature index and existing Fourier/free-reference discussions
  were searched for stress, conserved tensors and Wick flux. No precise
  existing specialized match was recorded. The elementary regulator, finite
  Wick sum and linear normalization argument are proved explicitly; no
  unsupported external result is used to replace them.

  Inspection used bounded <verbatim|rg>, <verbatim|sed>, <verbatim|cat>,
  <verbatim|wc -l> on the files named above. An initial guessed path
  <verbatim|FREE_STRESS/Choose.lean> did not exist; <verbatim|rg --files>
  located <verbatim|FREE_STRESS_CERTIFICATE/Choose.lean>, which was then
  read. No Lean build, axiom replay, or source changes. TeX/render checks and
  independent source/mathematical review are pending. All prose remains
  draft.

